             "A CURE THAT CAN ADD WHAT THE FLOOR NEVER HELD IS NOT A CURE: every marker repair is gated on the verse's own Hebrew. 1 Sam 9:26 carries ⟨ئەتكە⟩ where the Hebrew (ואשלחך) has no את at all. 11 rows refused. And mixed forms restore the BARE marker only — ⟨ئەتتى⟩ collapses to אתי ('with me') at 2 Chr 3:14 where the Hebrew is a bare את, so inventing a suffix is worse than not restoring one"
             "THE ERASURE IS A HEDGE-SHAPE WITH THREE HABITATS, not a word: bare in the flow apposed to the rail (Deut 5:9, Exod 3:18, and 2 Kgs 17:7 reaching for پەرۋەردىگار — a DIFFERENT title, so a cure keyed on خۇدا alone would miss it); inside a ⟨supplied-word⟩ bracket (Jer 46:18 ⟨خۇدا⟩); and WORST, erasure-primary with the rail parenthesised in the row only (2 Chr 35:3 אלהיכם → خۇدايۇلار (ئېلوھىڭلار), where the flow carries خۇدايۇلار alone and the reader receives only the erasure). 29 verses → 0; 26 cleared on a re-render at 48000/glm-5.3/0.7 because the erasure is a groove a different sample shakes loose"
             "SCOTT'S RULING 2026-09-17 — NO LATER PROPHETS IN THE TANAKH: پەيغەمبەر is Uyghur's ordinary word for prophet AND the word it uses for Muhammad. نەبى is cognate with נביא through נ-ב-א and carries no later figure into the text. 646 substitutions. The rule: a word a language reserves for a post-biblical figure never renders a Tanakh common noun, EVEN WHEN it is that language's ordinary word — the posture clause does not reach it"
             "A WORD LIST CAN NEVER BE THE DISCRIMINATOR, because every word a defect uses is also a word the text uses. رەب is legitimate inside ئەرەب (Arabia, glossing ערב), ئەرەبە (the Arabah), رەبكە and رەبقە (both Rebekah), گارەب (Gareb), تېرەبىنت (terebinth), يارەب (Yareb), ئورەب (Oreb), رەببەسى (Rabbah), and as the gloss of רב in Rab-saris. دېمە lives inside دېمەك and is the correct rendering of אל תאמר at Prov 20:22. The test is LICENSING: text in the flow with no surface behind it is the chair speaking; text a gloss also carries is translation"
             "THE MARKER GAP TRACKS THE BOOK, and the denominator matters as much as the gap: Lev 135/row315 · Isa 22/row59 · Ps 8/row23 · Prov 6/row12 · Chr 26/row83. Chronicles was predicted HIGHER and came in LOWER — that window is genealogy. The variable is CLAUSE DENSITY WITH DIRECT OBJECTS, not narrative-versus-poetry"
